    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>According to tradition Rome was founded in 753 BCE, while the archaeology shows villages on its hills joining into a city in the mid-8th century BCE.</li><li>It was capital of a kingdom, a republic and an empire, and then lost people and standing through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic Wars</a> and the centuries of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">Papacy</a>.</li><li>The popes made it the centre of the Papal States and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>, and it became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> in 1871.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Because Rome shrank so far in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, very significant ancient Roman remains survived in its centre, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocas">Phocas</a>'s gift of the Pantheon to the Pope probably saved it from destruction.</p></aside>
    </section>

